# Goodnotes

> Goodnotes is a note-taking app that combines natural handwriting with smart AI tools — helping people capture, organise, and develop their ideas across work, study, and everyday life.

Goodnotes was created in 2011 by Steven Chan and has grown into one of the top digital note-taking apps in the world, winning the Apple iPad App of the Year Award in 2022. It has 4.7 stars from over 381,000 App Store reviews. The app is available on iPad, iPhone, Mac, Android, Windows, and the web. Goodnotes is headquartered in London.

## Products

- [Goodnotes](https://www.goodnotes.com): The core note-taking and digital paper app, with AI features, PDF annotation, handwriting recognition, and cross-device sync.
- [Goodnotes Education](https://www.goodnotes.com/learning/education): An all-in-one space for K-12 schools built into the main app. Free for schools.
- [Goodnotes Teams](https://www.goodnotes.com/business): A team-ready version with MDM integration, admin console, and controls for enabling or disabling AI features.
- [Goodnotes Enterprise](https://www.goodnotes.com/business): A team-ready version with MDM integration, admin console, enterprise-based pricing, and controls for enabling or disabling AI features. Custom pricing available for 25 seats and up.

## Core tools and features

- Note-taking: a natural handwriting experience that feels like pen on paper.
- Whiteboard: an infinite canvas to create, plan, brainstorm and collaborate.
- AI-powered tools: Goodnotes AI, Spellcheck.
- Study Sets: create and study with flashcards and study materials.
- PDF import, annotation, highlighting, and markup.
- Handwriting recognition and OCR for searching handwritten notes, typed text, PDF content, and folder titles.
- Audio recording synced to the moment you write.
- Real-time collaboration and live sharing.
- Text documents, whiteboards, diagrams, and shape creation.
- Presentation Mode with Laser Pointer.
- Templates, covers, and folder organisation.
- Cross-platform sync (iCloud and Goodnotes cloud).
- Offline access.

